1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,466
I'm Peppa Pig!

2
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:05,399
[oinks]

3
00:00:05,466 --> 00:00:07,300
This is my little brother George.

4
00:00:07,366 --> 00:00:08,233
[oinks]

5
00:00:08,299 --> 00:00:09,500
This is Mommy Pig.

6
00:00:09,566 --> 00:00:10,433
[oinks]

7
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,200
And this is Daddy Pig.

8
00:00:12,266 --> 00:00:13,733
[oinks loudly then all laugh]

9
00:00:14,166 --> 00:00:15,266
Peppa Pig!

10
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:18,733
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

11
00:00:19,266 --> 00:00:22,599
[narrator] Peppa's family are on holiday
in their Camper Van.

12
00:00:22,666 --> 00:00:24,400
[rooster crowing]

13
00:00:24,766 --> 00:00:27,066
[Daddy Pig]
Good morning, my little piggies!

14
00:00:27,133 --> 00:00:29,133
[all] Good morning, Daddy Pig!

15
00:00:30,099 --> 00:00:32,133
I love camping!

16
00:00:32,199 --> 00:00:34,166
Since we're in the countryside,

17
00:00:34,233 --> 00:00:37,633
I thought we could spend the day
looking at nature.

18
00:00:37,699 --> 00:00:39,766
Good idea, Mommy Pig!

19
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,166
Let's watch a nature program.

20
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:45,466
[announcer]
One of the wonders of nature, birds.

21
00:00:46,466 --> 00:00:47,733
How lovely!

22
00:00:48,166 --> 00:00:49,500
[cawing]

23
00:00:49,566 --> 00:00:51,666
Shoosh! Shoosh, little birdie!

24
00:00:51,733 --> 00:00:54,033
We can't hear our TV.

25
00:00:54,533 --> 00:00:55,699
Oh, Daddy Pig!

26
00:00:56,066 --> 00:00:58,566
There's no point
being on a camping holiday

27
00:00:58,633 --> 00:01:00,533
and just watching TV.

28
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,666
We can do that at home!

29
00:01:02,733 --> 00:01:05,399
Uh, good thinking, Mommy Pig.

30
00:01:05,466 --> 00:01:08,166
There are lots of fun places we can visit.

31
00:01:08,633 --> 00:01:10,333
There's Tree World.

32
00:01:10,399 --> 00:01:12,466
What's Tree World?

33
00:01:12,533 --> 00:01:16,566
Tree World is a big forest, full of trees.

34
00:01:16,633 --> 00:01:19,333
It sounds a bit boring.

35
00:01:19,399 --> 00:01:21,233
Or there's Potato City.

36
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:23,500
What's Potato City?

37
00:01:23,733 --> 00:01:28,600
There's a tour of the potato fields,
ending with a potato tasting.

38
00:01:28,666 --> 00:01:30,566
Sounds interesting!

39
00:01:30,633 --> 00:01:32,466
Or there's Duck Land.

40
00:01:32,533 --> 00:01:34,300
What's Duck Land?

41
00:01:34,566 --> 00:01:37,766
It's a wide river, full of ducks.

42
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,266
Duck Land!

43
00:01:39,699 --> 00:01:41,766
Let's go to Duck Land!

44
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:42,733
[oinks]

45
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:45,266
[narrator] 
Peppa and George love ducks.

46
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:47,699
How do we get to Duck Land?

47
00:01:47,766 --> 00:01:49,633
The Camper Van can guide us.

48
00:01:50,199 --> 00:01:53,399
[female voice]
Hello. Where are we going today?

49
00:01:53,466 --> 00:01:55,733
Duck Land, please!

50
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:59,566
[female voice]
Follow the road ahead in a straight line.

51
00:01:59,633 --> 00:02:03,633
[all singing] We're going to Duck Land
In our Camper Van

52
00:02:04,233 --> 00:02:06,233
Welcome to Duck Land!

53
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:12,000
-How many tickets, please?
-Two adults and two children.

54
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:15,666
Enjoy the ducks!

55
00:02:17,533 --> 00:02:19,299
Where are the ducks?

56
00:02:19,366 --> 00:02:21,400
Maybe they're on holiday.

57
00:02:21,633 --> 00:02:24,233
Let's have our picnic lunch!

58
00:02:24,633 --> 00:02:28,766
-The ducks always turn up--
-When we have picnics!

59
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,000
[laughing]

60
00:02:30,066 --> 00:02:32,299
[narrator] 
Peppa and George love picnics.

61
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,466
[ducks quacking]

62
00:02:34,533 --> 00:02:36,533
Look! It's the ducks!

63
00:02:37,566 --> 00:02:41,266
Stop, Daddy! We need bread for the ducks!

64
00:02:41,466 --> 00:02:42,766
Huh? Oh, heh.

65
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:43,766
All right!

66
00:02:44,466 --> 00:02:46,100
Hello, Mrs. Duck!

67
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:48,366
[narrator] Here come more ducks.

68
00:02:48,433 --> 00:02:51,133
All their brothers and sisters are here!

69
00:02:51,733 --> 00:02:54,133
[narrator] And here come more ducks!

70
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:57,033
It's the Granny and Grandpa ducks!

71
00:02:57,333 --> 00:03:00,000
And here are all the Aunties and Uncles!

72
00:03:00,066 --> 00:03:01,233
[all quacking]

73
00:03:02,433 --> 00:03:04,600
That's the last of our picnic gone!

74
00:03:04,666 --> 00:03:07,666
Ducks, say thank you to Daddy Pig!

75
00:03:08,533 --> 00:03:11,700
Oh, ho! You're most welcome!

76
00:03:11,766 --> 00:03:14,733
Ha-ha-ha! I love Duck Land!

77
00:03:16,633 --> 00:03:18,433
[narrator] It is time to go home.

78
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:21,266
I wonder what's the shortest way home.

79
00:03:21,799 --> 00:03:25,533
[female voice]
Drive straight ahead into the river.

80
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Oh! Are you sure?

81
00:03:28,233 --> 00:03:31,600
[female voice] Yes. Drive into the river.

82
00:03:31,666 --> 00:03:33,799
But we can't drive in a river!

83
00:03:34,033 --> 00:03:36,666
Yes. It's talking nonsense!

84
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:39,766
[female voice]
Please press the blue button.

85
00:03:44,733 --> 00:03:47,466
[narrator]
The Camper Van is driving into the river!

86
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:52,200
Our Camper Van has turned into a boat!

87
00:03:52,266 --> 00:03:54,533
I wasn't quite expecting that.

88
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,600
[female voice]
Welcome to the car of the future.

89
00:03:58,366 --> 00:04:02,700
Look! It's Granddad Dog and Danny Dog!

90
00:04:02,766 --> 00:04:04,566
Ahoy there, Daddy Pig!

91
00:04:04,633 --> 00:04:06,766
[honking]

92
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,166
Uh... Ahoy there!

93
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:14,633
Sailing on the river
In our camper van

94
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:18,766
[female voice] Drive up the next hill.

95
00:04:20,333 --> 00:04:23,000
You have reached your destination.

96
00:04:23,066 --> 00:04:24,433
We're home!

97
00:04:25,366 --> 00:04:28,733
Thank you for a lovely holiday,
Mrs. Camper Van.

98
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:31,300
[female voice]
Ho, ho! You're most welcome.

99
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:37,533
It's nice going on holiday.

100
00:04:37,599 --> 00:04:40,666
But it's nicer to be back
in our own little house!

101
00:04:41,433 --> 00:04:43,666
[Daddy Pig] Good night, my little piggies!

102
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:44,800
[Peppa] Good night!

103
00:04:49,766 --> 00:04:53,300
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

104
00:04:55,599 --> 00:04:58,633
[narrator] Daddy Pig is making
vegetable soup for lunch.

105
00:04:59,466 --> 00:05:01,300
Daddy, can I help?

106
00:05:01,766 --> 00:05:05,300
Thank you, Peppa. Can you clear away
all these vegetable peelings?

107
00:05:05,366 --> 00:05:06,300
Okay! Ha-ha-ha.

108
00:05:07,099 --> 00:05:08,300
[Mommy Pig] Stop, Peppa!

109
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:11,633
Vegetable peelings don't go
in the normal bin.

110
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:13,666
They go in this brown bin.

111
00:05:14,266 --> 00:05:15,766
Ooh, na-na.

112
00:05:16,366 --> 00:05:19,466
That's right, George. It's a banana skin.

113
00:05:19,633 --> 00:05:21,633
And there are onions and carrots

114
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:25,033
and all sorts fruit
and vegetable leftovers in here.

115
00:05:25,099 --> 00:05:27,533
Granny and Grandpa will like these.

116
00:05:27,599 --> 00:05:32,566
Do Granny and Grandpa Pig
eat potato peelings?

117
00:05:32,633 --> 00:05:34,533
Ha-ha-ha. No, Peppa.

118
00:05:34,599 --> 00:05:38,133
They're for Grandpa's garden.
They help his plants grow.

119
00:05:39,766 --> 00:05:43,200
-We'll take these round there after lunch.
-Oh, goody!

120
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:47,500
[narrator] Mommy Pig, Peppa,
and George are taking the peelings

121
00:05:47,566 --> 00:05:49,633
over to Granny and Grandpa Pig's house.

122
00:05:50,033 --> 00:05:51,200
We're here!

123
00:05:51,599 --> 00:05:53,033
Hooray!

124
00:05:54,466 --> 00:05:57,166
-Grandpa Pig!
-Baba Ig!

125
00:05:57,233 --> 00:05:59,599
We've got a special present for you.

126
00:05:59,666 --> 00:06:02,800
Ah! Vegetable peelings!

127
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:04,599
Fantastic!

128
00:06:04,666 --> 00:06:06,800
My garden will like these.

129
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:10,133
Does your garden eat vegetables?

130
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:16,433
Ha, ha. No, Peppa, these peelings
are for my compost heap.

131
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:18,166
What's that?

132
00:06:18,233 --> 00:06:19,733
I'll show you.

133
00:06:19,799 --> 00:06:21,266
Here it is.

134
00:06:21,333 --> 00:06:23,266
It's a wooden box!

135
00:06:23,333 --> 00:06:28,333
Yes, Peppa,
but it's a very clever wooden box.

136
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:31,566
I put these peelings in the top,

137
00:06:31,633 --> 00:06:34,166
and then out of the bottom comes

138
00:06:34,233 --> 00:06:38,233
lovely rich earth called compost.

139
00:06:38,299 --> 00:06:40,166
How does it do that?

140
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:41,766
Is it a magic box?

141
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,166
[laughs]

142
00:06:43,233 --> 00:06:44,533
No, Peppa.

143
00:06:44,766 --> 00:06:49,166
I've got some little friends
that give it some help.

144
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:51,099
Where?

145
00:06:51,166 --> 00:06:53,566
In here. Look.

146
00:06:53,633 --> 00:06:56,133
Ah! Wriggly worms.

147
00:06:56,766 --> 00:06:58,166
Wiggle wiggle.

148
00:06:58,566 --> 00:07:02,133
[narrator] The worms turn all the fruit
and vegetables into compost.

149
00:07:02,599 --> 00:07:08,433
Grandpa, can we find some more
wriggly worms for your compost heap?

150
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:10,700
What a good idea.

151
00:07:11,166 --> 00:07:12,500
Come on, George!

152
00:07:12,566 --> 00:07:15,299
Let's find some more wriggly worms.

153
00:07:15,666 --> 00:07:17,466
[laughing]

154
00:07:19,299 --> 00:07:20,433
A wriggly worm!

155
00:07:21,133 --> 00:07:22,533
Wiggle wiggle!

156
00:07:22,599 --> 00:07:26,266
You're a wriggly worm
You're a wriggly worm

157
00:07:26,333 --> 00:07:29,233
How do you do?
I love you

158
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:31,700
You're a wriggly worm

159
00:07:31,766 --> 00:07:34,433
Ah-ha! Well done!

160
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:36,633
Be a good wriggly worm,

161
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:40,066
and turn it all into compost!

162
00:07:40,133 --> 00:07:41,333
[all laugh]

163
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,733
Then I can use the compost to--

164
00:07:44,799 --> 00:07:48,166
I know! I know!
You put a seed in the ground,

165
00:07:48,233 --> 00:07:51,333
cover it in compost,
and it grows into a tree.

166
00:07:52,666 --> 00:07:54,133
Yes, Peppa!

167
00:07:54,366 --> 00:07:56,299
And talking of trees,

168
00:07:56,366 --> 00:07:59,000
we'd better go and help Granny Pig.

169
00:07:59,066 --> 00:08:03,099
She's collecting fruit in the orchard.

170
00:08:03,166 --> 00:08:05,033
What's the orchard?

171
00:08:05,099 --> 00:08:07,066
It's where you find fruit trees.

172
00:08:07,366 --> 00:08:10,400
We've had this orchard
since I was a little piggy.

173
00:08:10,466 --> 00:08:13,666
-Hello, Granny Pig.
-Gangy Ig!

174
00:08:14,099 --> 00:08:16,766
-Are you going to help me collect apples?
-Yes, Granny!

175
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,066
Oh. The apples are too high up.

176
00:08:21,133 --> 00:08:22,299
Don't worry, Peppa.

177
00:08:22,566 --> 00:08:26,366
Granny and Grandpa have
a little trick to collect the apples.

178
00:08:26,433 --> 00:08:29,000
Everybody hold onto the tree.

179
00:08:29,433 --> 00:08:33,333
On the count of three,
shake the tree as much as you can.

180
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:36,666
One, two, three!

181
00:08:38,266 --> 00:08:41,100
It's raining apples!

182
00:08:43,133 --> 00:08:44,333
[laughs]

183
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,633
Granny, can we have an apple, please?

184
00:08:48,366 --> 00:08:49,466
Of course, Peppa.

185
00:08:51,633 --> 00:08:53,600
Delicious!

186
00:08:53,666 --> 00:08:58,233
And can you guess what we do
with the apple cores?

187
00:08:58,300 --> 00:08:59,500
Uh...

188
00:09:01,033 --> 00:09:03,233
-Wiggle wiggle!
-[narrator] That's right!

189
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:06,566
The apple cores go into the compost
for the worms.

190
00:09:06,633 --> 00:09:08,300
Clever George!

191
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:12,600
And clever wriggly worms, too!

192
00:09:12,666 --> 00:09:15,633
[all laughing]

193
00:09:20,333 --> 00:09:24,133
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

194
00:09:24,199 --> 00:09:27,100
[narrator] Peppa and George
are playing in their bedroom.

195
00:09:27,166 --> 00:09:29,433
This will be the best house ever!

196
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:30,633
[laughing]

197
00:09:30,699 --> 00:09:31,766
[door bell rings]

198
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,699
[Daddy Pig]
George! Richard Rabbit is here!

199
00:09:37,633 --> 00:09:40,000
-Georgie!
-Richard!

200
00:09:40,066 --> 00:09:42,533
-Dine-Saw!
-Dine-Saw!

201
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,699
Bye-bye, Richard.
I'll be back to pick you up later.

202
00:09:48,766 --> 00:09:51,066
[narrator]
George and Richard are friends.

203
00:09:51,133 --> 00:09:52,400
[laughing]

204
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,166
George! Richard!

205
00:09:58,366 --> 00:10:01,033
You've knocked my house down!

206
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:04,533
Please play something not bouncy.

207
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:11,766
[narrator] George has made the toy basket
into a volcano!

208
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:17,033
Richard is using toy trees
to make a jungle!

209
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:21,466
George has used the building blocks
to make a river!

210
00:10:21,533 --> 00:10:22,766
-Dine-Saw!
-Dine-Saw!

211
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,733
[narrator] George and Richard have turned
the bedroom into Dinosaur Land!

212
00:10:27,333 --> 00:10:30,600
I'm leaving! It's too noisy!

213
00:10:30,666 --> 00:10:34,433
-I say Po-tay-to
-And I say Po-tah-to

214
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:37,266
-Po-tay-to
-Po-tah-to

215
00:10:37,333 --> 00:10:42,366
The good thing about rainy days is
we get to watch important TV programs.

216
00:10:42,433 --> 00:10:44,033
-Po-tay-to!
-Po-tah-to!

217
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:45,500
-Po-tay-to!
-Po-tah-to!

218
00:10:45,566 --> 00:10:51,733
Mummy, George and Richard have
made the bedroom into Dinosaur Land.

219
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:54,699
And Dinosaur Land is very noisy.

220
00:10:55,266 --> 00:11:00,366
George has his best friend here,
but I've got no one to play with.

221
00:11:00,433 --> 00:11:03,400
You could ask Suzy Sheep to come over.

222
00:11:03,466 --> 00:11:05,800
[narrator] 
Suzy Sheep is Peppa's best friend.

223
00:11:06,033 --> 00:11:09,333
Can Suzy really come over now?

224
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:10,400
Let's ring her.

225
00:11:14,166 --> 00:11:15,466
[ringing]

226
00:11:17,166 --> 00:11:19,733
Hello, Suzy Sheep speaking.

227
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:22,233
Suzy, it's me.

228
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:24,666
Can you come to my house now?

229
00:11:24,733 --> 00:11:28,400
Yes, Peppa! Can I wear my nurse's costume?

230
00:11:28,466 --> 00:11:31,433
Yes, but come quickly.

231
00:11:38,199 --> 00:11:41,633
-Bye-bye, Suzy! I'll be back to...
-Quick, Suzy!

232
00:11:41,699 --> 00:11:43,633
...pick you up later.

233
00:11:46,566 --> 00:11:48,800
George! Richard!

234
00:11:49,033 --> 00:11:51,133
Nurse Suzy is here.

235
00:11:51,199 --> 00:11:55,533
And Nurse Suzy says,
this is not Dinosaur Land.

236
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:57,733
It is a hospital.

237
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:02,199
And a hospital must be clean and tidy.

238
00:12:02,266 --> 00:12:05,666
[narrator] 
The bedroom is not Dinosaur Land anymore.

239
00:12:05,733 --> 00:12:07,366
It is a hospital.

240
00:12:07,433 --> 00:12:09,666
I'm the important doctor.

241
00:12:10,166 --> 00:12:13,533
Mm. This dinosaur looks sick.

242
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:18,066
I agree, doctor.
He is a very greeny ill color.

243
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:20,433
He must go to bed.

244
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:25,166
And this dinosaur
is a very purple-y ill color.

245
00:12:25,233 --> 00:12:29,533
Yes, doctor. He must go into bed, too.

246
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:30,800
-Dine-Saw!
-Dine-Saw!

247
00:12:31,033 --> 00:12:34,333
Shush. Quiet in the hospital!

248
00:12:36,066 --> 00:12:37,333
Choo! Choo!

249
00:12:38,566 --> 00:12:41,333
[narrator] 
The bedroom is not a hospital anymore.

250
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:43,466
Now it is a railway station.

251
00:12:44,166 --> 00:12:49,199
No! No!
There aren't any trains in Fairy Land!

252
00:12:49,266 --> 00:12:52,266
[narrator]
Oh. Now the bedroom is Fairy Land.

253
00:12:52,333 --> 00:12:56,033
Only pretty things are allowed
in Fairy Land.

254
00:12:56,099 --> 00:12:57,666
[crying]

255
00:12:58,566 --> 00:13:00,599
What's all this crying about?

256
00:13:00,666 --> 00:13:04,800
George and Richard
want to play dinosaurs and trains.

257
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:09,566
And we want to play hospitals and fairies.

258
00:13:09,633 --> 00:13:13,699
Mm. I see the rain has stopped outside.

259
00:13:13,766 --> 00:13:19,199
-So?
-So, maybe you could all play outside.

260
00:13:19,266 --> 00:13:22,400
But they like little boys' games.

261
00:13:22,466 --> 00:13:25,699
And we like grown-up girls' games.

262
00:13:25,766 --> 00:13:30,766
But after it's been raining in the garden,
what do you normally find?

263
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:33,633
-Muddy...
-Puddles!

264
00:13:33,699 --> 00:13:36,699
And what are muddy puddles for?

265
00:13:36,766 --> 00:13:39,266
Jumping up and down in!

266
00:13:40,633 --> 00:13:43,766
[narrator] Everyone loves jumping
up and down in muddy puddles.

267
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:47,199
Whether they are big girls or little boys.

268
00:13:49,633 --> 00:13:51,633
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

269
00:13:51,699 --> 00:13:56,400
[narrator] It has been very stormy
weather, and the school roof is leaking.

270
00:13:56,466 --> 00:14:00,066
How can we raise the money
to fix the school roof?

271
00:14:00,466 --> 00:14:02,500
We could have a fun run!

272
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,000
What's a funny run?

273
00:14:05,066 --> 00:14:09,333
It's a day for picnics
and giving money to see people run.

274
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:12,166
And the more money you give,
the further they run.

275
00:14:12,233 --> 00:14:16,199
Good idea, Daddy Pig.
How far can you run?

276
00:14:16,266 --> 00:14:18,099
What? Uh...

277
00:14:18,166 --> 00:14:20,500
Well, I can run as far as you like.

278
00:14:20,566 --> 00:14:23,533
But, Daddy, you can hardly run at all!

279
00:14:23,599 --> 00:14:25,066
Nonsense!

280
00:14:25,466 --> 00:14:28,000
-I'm an expert at running.
-Good.

281
00:14:28,466 --> 00:14:31,566
-Does anyone else want to run?
-No, thank you.

282
00:14:32,433 --> 00:14:35,166
But I'll give money to see Daddy Pig run!

283
00:14:35,233 --> 00:14:37,000
-Me, too!
-And me!

284
00:14:37,066 --> 00:14:40,266
Excellent! Thank you, Daddy Pig!

285
00:14:41,666 --> 00:14:44,333
[narrator]
Peppa and her family are eating spaghetti.

286
00:14:45,533 --> 00:14:48,166
Delicious! Is there any more spaghetti?

287
00:14:48,633 --> 00:14:52,166
Daddy Pig!
You've already had three helpings!

288
00:14:52,233 --> 00:14:53,766
Eating gives me energy.

289
00:14:54,333 --> 00:14:56,733
And I need energy for my fun run!

290
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:59,533
You also need to practice running!

291
00:14:59,599 --> 00:15:04,400
What if I practice eating today,
then practice running tomorrow?

292
00:15:04,466 --> 00:15:08,500
No, Daddy!
You need to practice running now!

293
00:15:08,566 --> 00:15:12,033
-Oh.
-Come on, Daddy, race you!

294
00:15:13,199 --> 00:15:14,500
This is easy!

295
00:15:14,566 --> 00:15:16,699
[narrator]
It is easy to run downhill.

296
00:15:18,266 --> 00:15:20,433
It is hard to run uphill.

297
00:15:21,066 --> 00:15:24,333
I don't think I should have eaten
so much spaghetti.

298
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:26,533
[bell ringing]

299
00:15:26,599 --> 00:15:28,599
[narrator]
It is the day of the fun run.

300
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:33,666
Madame Gazelle has a chart
to show how far Daddy Pig must run.

301
00:15:33,733 --> 00:15:36,300
If Daddy Pig can run to here...

302
00:15:36,599 --> 00:15:38,199
The supermarket!

303
00:15:38,266 --> 00:15:39,400
...then to here...

304
00:15:39,599 --> 00:15:41,733
My Granddad's garage!

305
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:44,133
...and all the way to here...

306
00:15:44,199 --> 00:15:45,666
Windy Castle!

307
00:15:45,733 --> 00:15:49,800
...then we'll have enough money
to fix the school roof!

308
00:15:50,433 --> 00:15:52,099
I'll do it now.

309
00:15:52,166 --> 00:15:54,466
Ready, steady, go!

310
00:15:55,733 --> 00:15:58,466
I did it! Now we can have the picnic!

311
00:15:58,533 --> 00:16:02,800
Ha, ha. Silly Daddy!
That's just a drawing.

312
00:16:03,033 --> 00:16:06,766
Yes. Now you must run
to the real Windy Castle.

313
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,199
Oh.

314
00:16:08,266 --> 00:16:12,000
-Ready, steady, go!
-Hooray!

315
00:16:13,699 --> 00:16:17,266
Huff, puff, huff, puff.

316
00:16:17,333 --> 00:16:20,533
Come on, Daddy Pig, you can make it!

317
00:16:25,533 --> 00:16:28,633
Come on, bus, you can make it!

318
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:32,199
[narrator] The school bus has made it
to Windy Castle.

319
00:16:32,766 --> 00:16:35,466
Now everyone can enjoy the picnic.

320
00:16:36,066 --> 00:16:38,633
Water! Water!

321
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:42,033
What a lovely hot day.

322
00:16:42,099 --> 00:16:45,466
And such a relaxing way
to raise money, too.

323
00:16:46,233 --> 00:16:48,400
Water! Water!

324
00:16:48,599 --> 00:16:51,366
[narrator]
Daddy Pig has reached the Supermarket.

325
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:54,766
All the running has made him very thirsty.

326
00:16:58,666 --> 00:17:01,199
Let's look through the telescope!

327
00:17:01,533 --> 00:17:03,400
I can see Daddy!

328
00:17:03,466 --> 00:17:06,166
[narrator] The telescope
makes everything look closer.

329
00:17:06,233 --> 00:17:09,200
[Peppa] Oh, he's not going very fast.

330
00:17:09,666 --> 00:17:12,599
[narrator] Daddy Pig has arrived
at Granddad Dog's garage.

331
00:17:12,666 --> 00:17:15,233
That's it. I can't go on.

332
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:17,433
Daddy has stopped!

333
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:18,633
[all] Aww.

334
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:20,766
You look rather hot.

335
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:24,766
You need something to cool you down
and give you energy.

336
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,500
Have an ice lolly!

337
00:17:26,566 --> 00:17:28,566
Thank you, Granddad Dog!

338
00:17:30,600 --> 00:17:32,066
That's nice!

339
00:17:32,133 --> 00:17:34,000
Aah! A wasp!

340
00:17:34,066 --> 00:17:37,266
Shoo! Shoo! Get away, you little pest!

341
00:17:37,333 --> 00:17:40,233
[narrator] The wasp wants to share
Daddy Pig's ice lolly.

342
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:43,166
No! This is my lolly.

343
00:17:43,233 --> 00:17:47,166
Daddy's started running again,
really fast!

344
00:17:47,233 --> 00:17:48,800
Hooray!

345
00:17:49,033 --> 00:17:50,800
[screaming]

346
00:17:51,033 --> 00:17:52,800
Get off! Get off!

347
00:17:53,033 --> 00:17:55,366
You can stop now, Daddy Pig!

348
00:17:55,433 --> 00:17:58,333
We have enough money
to fix the school roof!

349
00:17:58,399 --> 00:18:00,333
[screaming]

350
00:18:01,166 --> 00:18:03,200
[narrator]
Daddy Pig has lost the wasp.

351
00:18:03,666 --> 00:18:05,700
Well done, Daddy Pig!

352
00:18:06,133 --> 00:18:08,000
All that extra running means

353
00:18:08,066 --> 00:18:11,733
we've got enough money
for a new school bus, too!

354
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:13,433
Thank you, Daddy Pig!

355
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:14,633
Oh? Oh.

356
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:16,633
You're most welcome.

357
00:18:16,700 --> 00:18:18,233
[all laughing]

358
00:18:21,533 --> 00:18:24,333
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

359
00:18:26,166 --> 00:18:28,800
[narrator] Daddy Pig is doing the washing
this morning.

360
00:18:30,233 --> 00:18:32,633
Daddy, what's that shirt?

361
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:35,600
It's my football shirt.

362
00:18:35,666 --> 00:18:38,466
Daddy's playing football this afternoon.

363
00:18:38,533 --> 00:18:39,533
Ooh.

364
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:41,700
But first, I have to go to work.

365
00:18:42,733 --> 00:18:45,666
-See you later! Bye.
-Bye-bye.

366
00:18:47,766 --> 00:18:51,700
Poor Daddy. Having to go to work.

367
00:18:51,766 --> 00:18:54,033
Ah. Poor Daddy.

368
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:57,133
Come on, let's play!

369
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:58,800
Yes, let's play.

370
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:06,200
[narrator] Peppa loves jumping up and down
in muddy puddles.

371
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:10,066
George loves jumping up and down
in muddy puddles.

372
00:19:10,466 --> 00:19:14,500
Mommy Pig loves jumping up and down
in muddy puddles!

373
00:19:18,233 --> 00:19:19,500
Oh, dear.

374
00:19:20,033 --> 00:19:25,066
Mommy! We've splashed
Daddy's football shirt with mud!

375
00:19:26,033 --> 00:19:28,366
Don't worry. We'll just wash it.

376
00:19:28,433 --> 00:19:29,500
[laughs]

377
00:19:29,566 --> 00:19:34,200
It'll be washed in no time,
and Daddy won't know it was ever muddy.

378
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:38,766
Let's find some more things
to put in the machine.

379
00:19:39,600 --> 00:19:42,700
Oh, my dress is a bit muddy.

380
00:19:45,466 --> 00:19:48,700
[narrator] Mommy Pig and George
have found more things to wash.

381
00:19:48,766 --> 00:19:50,433
Very good, George.

382
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:55,700
We put the clothes in here...
and then, we switch it on.

383
00:19:56,600 --> 00:20:00,433
[narrator] The washing machine
is filling up with hot soapy water.

384
00:20:03,566 --> 00:20:06,633
Splosh, splosh, splosh.

385
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:09,433
Splosh, splosh, splosh.

386
00:20:12,733 --> 00:20:16,266
[narrator] The washing machine
is making the whole room shake!

387
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,133
Oh, Peppa, where's your dress?

388
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:22,700
I'm washing it!

389
00:20:22,766 --> 00:20:23,666
What?

390
00:20:24,233 --> 00:20:25,733
Oh, no!

391
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:33,766
Look, Mummy,
my red dress is all nice and clean.

392
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:38,433
Yes, Peppa, but look what it's done
to everything else!

393
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:39,500
[narrator] Oh, dear!

394
00:20:39,566 --> 00:20:43,066
Peppa's red dress
has made all the white clothes pink!

395
00:20:43,533 --> 00:20:47,266
Pink isn't a very good color
for a football shirt.

396
00:20:47,333 --> 00:20:48,399
Ooh.

397
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:51,166
[narrator] Daddy Pig is home from work.

398
00:20:51,766 --> 00:20:53,233
Hello, everyone!

399
00:20:53,300 --> 00:20:54,600
Hello, Daddy.

400
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:59,666
Uh, Daddy Pig, we've got
a bit of a problem, and...

401
00:20:59,733 --> 00:21:03,566
Tell me later, Mommy Pig.
I've got to get ready for football.

402
00:21:04,166 --> 00:21:06,700
-Now, where's my football shirt?
-Here.

403
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:11,100
Don't be silly, Peppa.
That's one of Mummy's dresses.

404
00:21:11,166 --> 00:21:12,100
It's pink!

405
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:16,433
No, Daddy. It's your football shirt.

406
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:19,266
It got a bit muddy.

407
00:21:19,333 --> 00:21:21,066
So, we washed it.

408
00:21:21,133 --> 00:21:25,033
And it all went a bit wrong.
Sorry, Daddy.

409
00:21:25,100 --> 00:21:28,333
But I can't wear a pink football shirt!

410
00:21:28,399 --> 00:21:32,200
Why not, Daddy? Pink is a lovely color!

411
00:21:32,266 --> 00:21:33,433
Hmm.

412
00:21:33,766 --> 00:21:36,433
-What do you think, George?
-Yuck!

413
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:39,033
[narrator] George does not like pink!

414
00:21:39,100 --> 00:21:40,466
[door bell rings]

415
00:21:40,533 --> 00:21:42,433
[narrator] Here are Daddy Pig's friends,

416
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:46,000
Mr. Bull, Mr. Rabbit,
Mr. Pony, and Mr. Zebra.

417
00:21:46,066 --> 00:21:47,266
Moo!

418
00:21:47,333 --> 00:21:49,766
Is Daddy Pig coming out to play?

419
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:51,600
He'll just be a moment.

420
00:21:51,666 --> 00:21:53,700
My team are in white.

421
00:21:54,166 --> 00:21:56,433
I need a white shirt!

422
00:21:56,500 --> 00:21:59,399
But, Daddy, you have a white shirt.

423
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:02,033
Just take off your jacket.

424
00:22:02,766 --> 00:22:05,666
-See?
-Fantastic!

425
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,566
Thank you, Peppa.

426
00:22:08,700 --> 00:22:11,333
-Hello, everyone.
-Hello, Daddy Pig.

427
00:22:11,399 --> 00:22:14,266
-Like your shirt.
-Very smart!

428
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:18,166
Thank you. Come on! Let's play football!

429
00:22:18,233 --> 00:22:19,333
Yes!

430
00:22:23,466 --> 00:22:25,733
-Goal!
-Hooray!

431
00:22:25,800 --> 00:22:28,366
-Hooray!
-Daddy!

432
00:22:28,433 --> 00:22:31,366
You've made your shirt all muddy!

433
00:22:31,433 --> 00:22:34,000
Ha-ha-ha. Of course, Peppa!

434
00:22:34,066 --> 00:22:37,466
Football shirts are meant to be muddy!

435
00:22:37,533 --> 00:22:39,266
[oinks loudly then Peppa laughs]

436
00:22:41,300 --> 00:22:43,666
[narrator]
Daddy Pig loves playing football.

437
00:22:43,733 --> 00:22:46,100
Everyone loves playing football.

438
00:22:46,166 --> 00:22:48,466
Especially when its muddy.

439
00:22:48,533 --> 00:22:49,500
[all laughing]

